+## Run without llama-swap
+
+Use this only when the DSH language-model provider is remote, on another GPU, or
+otherwise guaranteed not to consume the GPU used by ComfyUI:
+
+```yaml
+- id: dsh-director
+  config:
+    llmHandoffMode: comfy-only
+```
+
+`comfy-only` never resolves or contacts `llamaSwapBaseUrl`. Managed submission
+queues and monitors ComfyUI, concludes the active LLM turn, and settles as soon as
+terminal ComfyUI history is available; it does not pause native sends, call
+ComfyUI `/free`, show a VRAM release control, or wait for physical VRAM headroom.
+The default `llama-swap` mode is unchanged and remains required when both model
+runtimes share a GPU. Do not use a fake llama-swap endpoint to bypass shared-GPU
+coordination.
